abb — OpenMandriva package build client

abb works with RPM package repositories in OpenMandrivaAssociation on GitHub
and with OpenMandriva's Automated Build Farm (ABF). Use `abb build` to run
rpmbuild on your machine or `abb send` to submit a build to ABF. The client
also manages source files in the OpenMandriva file store and sends
publication requests for ABF builds.

Build locally
-------------

For example, clone the zlib packaging repository and build its RPMs.

    abb clone zlib branch=
    cd zlib
    abb build

`clone` uses the OpenMandrivaAssociation GitHub organization. The defaults
are `branch=master`, `remote=origin` and `restore=always`. An empty `branch=`
keeps the branch checked out by `git clone`. Use `restore=ask` to confirm
before restoring sources or `restore=none` to skip that step.

`build` runs rpmbuild in a package checkout with one spec file. Its default
action is `-bb` (build binary RPMs). Command suffixes select other actions,
for example `builda` for `-ba` and `buildp` for `-bp`. Extra rpmbuild flags
can follow the command, as in `abb buildi --short-circuit`. Build output
is saved to a `.buildlog` file by default (`buildlog=yes`).

Submit a build to ABF
---------------------

You need an ABF account with permission to build the project. From a package
checkout, submit a test build for the usual OpenMandriva architectures with
automatic publication disabled.

    abb send arch="x86_64 znver1 aarch64" publish=false

`send` takes at most one project name. With no name, abb infers the project
from the checkout. ABF builds the specified Git branch or commit, so push
any local packaging changes before submitting. On success, abb prints an
ABF build-list ID for each accepted request.

OpenMandriva typically builds for `x86_64`, `znver1` and `aarch64`. The
built-in list also includes `i686` and `armv7hnl`, which OpenMandriva rarely
targets. Pass multiple targets as a quoted, space-separated `arch` value.
abb resolves architecture names against the ABF server's architecture list.

Built-in defaults for `send`

    arch="i686 x86_64 armv7hnl aarch64 znver1"
    platform=cooker
    publish=true

`platform` selects the remote ABF build platform. `publish=true` requests
automatic publication of successful builds. Use `publish=false` for a build
you want to inspect before publishing.

Other submission options

    branch=master      Git branch to build.
    commit=            Use a full commit hash instead of the branch.
    repos=             Repositories to include, for example main,contrib.
    reposave=          Destination in platform/repo form. If omitted, abb
                       uses the project's repository for the build platform.
    updatetype=security
                       Update type. Other values are bugfix, enhancement,
                       recommended and newpackage.
    withrequired=false
                       Set to true to request a rebuild of reverse dependencies.

Use the ABF build lists page to check a build.
https://abf.openmandriva.org/build_lists

Command reference
-----------------

    abb clone <project> ...
        Clone one or more package repositories.

    abb new <project>
        Initialize a local Git repository with an origin URL. If the spec
        skeleton is readable, create <project>.spec from it. Override the
        default skeleton at /usr/share/abb/spek.skel with `defaultspec`.

    abb build [<project> ...]
        Restore sources according to `restore` and run rpmbuild locally.
        With no project argument, build from the current directory.

    abb restore [<project> ...]
        Download missing files listed in .abf.yml from
        https://file-store.openmandriva.org and check their SHA-1 sums.
        With no project argument, use the current directory.

    abb store <file> ...
        Run from the package checkout. Upload source files to the OpenMandriva
        file store and record their names and SHA-1 sums in .abf.yml.

    abb send [<project>]
        Submit remote build requests to ABF.

    abb view [<project>|<build-list-id>]
        Open a package repository on GitHub or an ABF build-list page in w3m.

    abb status [<project>]
        Uses lynx to query a build-list path under the GitHub project URL.
        That path returns 404 for OpenMandriva projects such as zlib. Use the
        ABF build lists page to check their build status.

    abb publish <build-list-id> ...
    abb rejectpublish <build-list-id> ...
        Request publication or reject publication of the specified ABF builds.

    abb vars [<setting> ...]
        Print effective settings. For example, `abb vars arch platform publish`
        shows the targets, platform and publication setting `send` would use.

Configuration
-------------

abb reads Bash assignments from ~/.abbrc, or from .abbrc in the current
directory if ~/.abbrc is absent. Pass supported settings as `name=value`
arguments to override the configuration file for one invocation.

The ABF API defaults to `https://abf.openmandriva.org/api/v1`.
Set `owner` to the project owner in ABF (default `openmandriva`). The
`abfyml` setting selects the source manifest (default `.abf.yml`).
